# A config change of `editor.tab_width` moves the width in a buffer
# that took the config's, and not in one whose `.editorconfig` named
# one or that `:setlocal` gave its own. The runner never loads config
# files, so this changes it with `:set ts` — the same
# `App.syncBufferPrefs` a reload runs (its unit test in `app.zig`
# reloads a workspace config). The tab opens with an indent guide
# (`│`); the letter lands at the width.
write .editorconfig "[*.mk]\ntab_width = 6\n"
write a.txt "\tA\n"
write b.txt "\tB\n"
write c.mk "\tC\n"
open c.mk
expect screen contains "1 │     C"
open a.txt
expect screen contains "1 │   A"
open b.txt
ex setlocal ts=2
expect screen contains "1 │ B"
ex set ts=8
expect screen contains "1 │ B"
open a.txt
expect screen contains "1 │       A"
open c.mk
expect screen contains "1 │     C"
open b.txt
expect screen contains "1 │ B"
